  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "# Issue\nAs it stands, Meta Quest's handling of multiple build channels is **subpar**. Due to synchronization bugs, [users may be stuck on a particular channel without additional care](https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/quest-provide-advanced-channel-switching-instructions).\n \nAdditionally, for those developing content for upcoming features, or providing testing for any particular Open Beta, but whom wish to continue using VRChat LIVE to play or interact with friends and peers, channel switching can be a particular hastle, requiring frequent wait times as the channel synchronizes, ADB tricks to forcefully downgrade the version using a backup of the APK; or completely reinstalling VRChat, requiring long-time users to completely reconfigure their controls, settings, safeties, pinned searches, and forcing the user to go through a tutorial despite their playtime.\nFurthermore, **exiting the beta channels when the Open Beta closes can sometimes fail, as the channel selection is no longer available, but the desired selection is retained, thus forcefully updating users to the next Open Beta when it is launched, without their consent.**\n \n# Remedy\nHost VRChat Open Beta as a separate listing within the Meta/Oculus store.\nBy providing a separate listing:\n1. Users wishing to try the beta will not have worry that they are \"stuck\" on a particular channel.\n2. Developers will be able to seamlessly switch between the beta and live channels without hastle.\n3. **When betas close the Open Beta listing can be updated with live channel updates, keeping in sync with the LIVE channel.**\n4. Users will not be at risk of being updated to future betas when previous betas close.",
